<title>GERMANY: TABLE-Ifo details German 1997, 1998 forecasts.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Ifo details German 1997, 1998 forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>DRESDEN, Germany 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a table of economic forecasts for Germany for 1997 and 1998 by the Munich-based Ifo economic research institute. Forecasts refer to pan-Germany unless otherwise stated. Percentage changes compare with previous year.</p>
<p>				     1996	  1997	  1998</p>
<p>Unemployment (jobless total) 3,965,000   4,335,000   4,260,000</p>
<p>Unemployment rate		10.3 pct    11.3 pct    11.1 pct</p>
<p>--West Germany jobless total 2,796,000   3,020,000   2,890,000</p>
<p>  Unemployment rate	    9.0 pct     9.8 pct     9.3 pct</p>
<p>--East Germany jobless total 1,169,000   1,315,000   1,370,000</p>
<p>  Unemployment rate	    15.7 pct    17.7 pct    18.4 pct</p>
<p>Gross domestic product growth 1.4 pct    2.25 pct    2.75 pct</p>
<p>--West Germany		    1.3 pct    2.25 pct    2.75 pct</p>
<p>--East Germany		    2.0 pct    2.0 pct     2.5 pct</p>
<p>Budget deficit/GDP ratio	3.8 pct    3.3 pct     2.6 pct</p>
<p>Private consumption (real)    +1.3 pct   +1.0 pct    +2.0 pct</p>
<p>State consumption		 +2.4 pct   +1.5 pct    +1.0 pct</p>
<p>Capital investment		-0.8 pct   +0.5 pct    +2.0 pct</p>
<p>--equipment spending	    +2.4 pct   +3.5 pct    +6.0 pct</p>
<p>--construction spending	 -2.7 pct   -2.0 pct    -0.5 pct</p>
<p>Domestic demand		   +0.8 pct   +1.0 pct    +2.0 pct</p>
<p>Exports			     +4.9 pct   +8.5 pct    +6.5 pct</p>
<p>Imports			     +2.6 pct   +4.0 pct    +5.0 pct</p>
<p>Consumer prices (approximate, average)   +1.75 pct   +2 pct</p>
<p>--David Crossland, Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
